-25c11c743e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e04df09-fefe-577f-8fc1-5bfd603147f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433183} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3eaffe6-2697-5bc4-b914-38bd0d4c4c37" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "affee19e-8bbb-5e06-bea1-1923b23ecbed" :question/math-academy-id "q-331903" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-7{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ {{field-3}}=-5{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-7{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-5{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-7L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-5L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=-7{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+6=-5{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b33fffb-189c-5d9f-921e-fb455c3f6d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b33fffb-189c-5d9f-921e-fb455c3f6d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433190} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb29a18-3baa-5257-96e8-ae32828c5d44" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9551a40-c332-54a5-8337-fb6b102278bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-332029" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=2{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+6=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)=3 \\\\ 2{X}_{1}(s)+(s-1){X}_{2}(s)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[\\frac{-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2}]+{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ (s-2)[-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =6 \\\\ -6(s-2)-(s-2)(s-1){X}_{2}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) & =6 \\\\ [-(s-2)(s-1)+2]{X}_{2}(s) & =6+6(s-2) \\\\ (-{s}^{2}+3s){X}_{2}(s) & =6s-6 \\\\ -s(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =6(s-1) \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-6-(s-1){X}_{2}(s)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-(s-1)(\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+\\frac{6(s-1)^{2}}{s(s-3)}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6s(s-3)+6(s-1)^{2}}{2s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(s+1)}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-6(s-1)}{s(s-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40121c1-ccf7-5696-91b5-0982718db94c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b40121c1-ccf7-5696-91b5-0982718db94c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303571} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e82724a-0d12-56e5-a64d-e4adc31f8e52" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad4202e-4528-57fc-b977-aa5764d31dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad4202e-4528-57fc-b977-aa5764d31dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302528} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa7dada-4bdf-567d-b0cf-41938cbd0a4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304506} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3359fe31-f29d-5b88-9305-ae6477f60c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3359fe31-f29d-5b88-9305-ae6477f60c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302773} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8304b86-242a-5737-8651-1ffde5f97851" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b10fe6-8a1a-529e-8b7b-9217cea22e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10b10fe6-8a1a-529e-8b7b-9217cea22e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302566} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8e1d37f-459d-53b0-945b-abafb595373e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8583693b-a733-5fca-ba20-8078cfaf6308" :question/math-academy-id "q-332391" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
